{"step_index":491,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-17T11:53:43Z","content":"The playbook [`playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml`](file:///home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml) has been crafted, tested, and validated end-to-end against live infrastructure (`mtq-mailsrvp-01`).\n\n---\n\n### Architecture & Execution Flow\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    A[\"ansible-playbook playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml\"] --> B[\"Phase 1: import_playbook: bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml\"]\n    B --> C[\"SSHD inspection & AllowGroups check\"]\n    C --> D[\"User koby-bowser-ansible & Passwordless Sudo (/etc/sudoers.d)\"]\n    D --> E[\"Deploy SSH Public Key (~/.ssh/authorized_keys & centralized path)\"]\n    E --> F[\"Phase 2: Web Server & TLS Discovery Engine\"]\n    F --> G[\"Detect Installation & Active State (Nginx / Apache2 / HTTPD)\"]\n    G --> H[\"Extract VirtualHosts, Hosted Domains, Listening Ports\"]\n    H --> I[\"Resolve On-Disk TLS Cert Paths & Parse Expiry / SANs via OpenSSL\"]\n    I --> J[\"Per-Host Detailed Audit Cards\"]\n    I --> K[\"Consolidated Multi-Host Infrastructure Summary Table\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n### Playbook Highlights\n\n1. **Phase 1 Bootstrap Integration**:\n   - Uses `ansible.builtin.import_playbook: bootstrap-koby-bowser.yml` as the first play.\n   - Automatically handles Debian/CentOS quirks, dynamic `AllowGroups` discovery (e.g. `SSH_Users`), centralized vs. local `authorized_keys`, and passwordless sudo.\n\n2. **Phase 2 Non-Destructive Deep Inspection**:\n   - Embedded self-contained Python discovery engine running under `become: true`.\n   - **Nginx inspection**: parses live dump (`nginx -T`) and filesystem configs (`/etc/nginx/sites-enabled/*`, `/etc/nginx/conf.d/*`), extracting `server_name`, `listen` directives, `ssl_certificate`, and `ssl_certificate_key`.\n   - **Apache / HTTPD inspection**: parses VirtualHost blocks across `/etc/apache2/sites-enabled/*` and `/etc/httpd/conf.d/*`, extracting `ServerName`, `ServerAlias`, `SSLCertificateFile`, and `SSLCertificateKeyFile`.\n   - **Certificate Deep Dive**: runs `openssl x509` against every on-disk certificate to extract expiration dates, days remaining, Subject CN, Issuer, an\n<truncated 1986 bytes>\n  Issuer     : C=US, O=Let's Encrypt, CN=YE1\n        Expires    : Nov 15 11:48:08 2026 GMT\n        SANs       : postfix.outremer-telecom.fr\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n```\n\n#### 2. Consolidated Summary Table\n```text\n================================================================================================================================================================\nINFRASTRUCTURE WEB & TLS CERTIFICATE SUMMARY TABLE\n================================================================================================================================================================\nHOST                 | SERVER   | HOSTED DOMAIN(S)                    | PORT(S)      | TLS CERTIFICATE PATH                   | STATUS / EXPIRY         \n----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n172.30.39.153        | nginx    | _ (default / catch-all)             | 80 defaul... | None                                   | No TLS                  \n172.30.39.153        | nginx    | 172.30.39.153, postfix.outremer-... | 80           | None                                   | No TLS                  \n172.30.39.153        | nginx    | 172.30.39.153, postfix.outremer-... | 443 ssl      | /etc/ssl/certs/postfix.pem             | VALID (58 days left)    \n================================================================================================================================================================\n```\n\n---\n\n### Playbook Source\n\nFile location: [`/home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml`](file:///home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml)\n\nTo run it against any inventory or group:\n```bash\nansible-playbook -i inventories/prod/hosts.yml playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml --limit <group_or_host>\n```\n\nWould you like me to commit [`playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml`](file:///home/koby/LINUX/playbooks/audit-web-certs.yml) to the `Baba-Koby` branch?","thinking":"The specified playbook integrates the passwordless SSH configuration through a direct import, addressing the first requirement. The core functionality now includes the necessary checks to determine the presence of web server software. The implementation on the live server shows the logic is correct and fully operational.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
